<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maha Sura Singhanat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1744–1803</span> · Also known as Chao Phraya Surasi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maha Sura Singhanat, born Bunma and known in the Thonburi period as Chao Phraya Surasi, was a Siamese general and the younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama-i">Rama I</a>. With his brother he led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taksin">Taksin</a>'s campaigns against Lan Na, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a>, including the capture of Vientiane in 1779. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama">Rama</a> I founded the Chakri dynasty in 1782 he became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/front-palace">Front Palace</a>, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>, and led the defence against the Burmese in the Nine Armies' War of 1785–1786.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maha-sura-singhanat.jpg" alt="Maha Sura Singhanat" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maha_Sura_Singhanat.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
